{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":904,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:Prov.17","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"Proverbs","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"Proverbs 17","reference":"Proverbs 17","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"4.","sourceParagraph":1,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":2,"text":"False lips - To false accusations and calumnies, which give him occasion and encouragement to do mischief.","sourceParagraph":1,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":3,"text":"7.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":4,"text":"Excellent speech - Discourse of high and excellent things.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":5,"text":"8.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":6,"text":"A precious stone - Pleasant and acceptable; and withal dazzles his eyes.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":7,"text":"Whithersoever - To whomsoever it is presented.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":8,"text":"But this, as also many of her Proverbs, are to be understood of most men, not of all.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":9,"text":"9.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":10,"text":"Covereth - That conceals as far as he may, other mens faults.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":9,"scriptureVerseEnd":9},{"verse":11,"text":"11.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":12,"text":"Rebellion - Against God.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":13,"text":"Messenger - Or, a cruel angel, the angel of death, the devil, or some bloody men employed by God to avenge his quarrel.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":11,"scriptureVerseEnd":11},{"verse":14,"text":"12.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":15,"text":"Folly - In the heat of his lust or passion.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":12,"scriptureVerseEnd":12},{"verse":16,"text":"14.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":17,"text":"Letteth out - By cutting the bank of a river.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":18,"text":"Leave off - Avoid the occasions, and prevent the beginning of contention.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":14,"scriptureVerseEnd":14},{"verse":19,"text":"16.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":20,"text":"A price - Opportunities and abilities of getting it.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":21,"text":"No heart - Neither discretion to discern the worth of wisdom, nor any sincere desire to get it.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":22,"text":"17.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":23,"text":"Was born - Was sent into the world for this, that he might comfort and relieve his brother in adversity.","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":17,"scriptureVerseEnd":17},{"verse":24,"text":"18.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":18,"scriptureVerseEnd":18},{"verse":25,"text":"Friend - Debtor, for whom being his friend, he becomes surety.","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":18,"scriptureVerseEnd":18},{"verse":26,"text":"20.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":20,"scriptureVerseEnd":20},{"verse":27,"text":"No good - Shall not get that advantage which he expects.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":20,"scriptureVerseEnd":20},{"verse":28,"text":"22.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":22,"scriptureVerseEnd":22},{"verse":29,"text":"Doth good - Even to the body; it contributes much to bodily health and vigour.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":22,"scriptureVerseEnd":22},{"verse":30,"text":"Drieth - Wastes the marrow of the bones, and the moisture and strength of the body.","sourceParagraph":12,"scriptureVerseStart":22,"scriptureVerseEnd":22},{"verse":31,"text":"24.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":24,"scriptureVerseEnd":24},{"verse":32,"text":"In the face - His wisdom appears even in his looks.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":24,"scriptureVerseEnd":24},{"verse":33,"text":"The eyes - Minding most, those things which are remotest from him, and least concern him.","sourceParagraph":13,"scriptureVerseStart":24,"scriptureVerseEnd":24},{"verse":34,"text":"26.","sourceParagraph":14,"scriptureVerseStart":26,"scriptureVerseEnd":26},{"verse":35,"text":"To strike - Nor to smite magistrates, either with the hand or tongue, for the execution of justice.","sourceParagraph":14,"scriptureVerseStart":26,"scriptureVerseEnd":26}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Proverbs","chapter":17}}